# Replace variables with isolated integration fixtures. Never commit actual tokens.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@buyerToken = REPLACE_BUYER_TOKEN
@recipientToken = REPLACE_RECIPIENT_TOKEN
@bookingId = REPLACE_BOOKING_UUID
@participantId = REPLACE_PARTICIPANT_UUID
@invitationId = REPLACE_INVITATION_UUID_FROM_CREATE
@recipientEmail = recipient@example.test
@createKey = public-invitation-test-001

### Buyer sends (retry with same key/body; for a new invitation use a new key)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/participants/{{participantId}}/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{createKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"recipientEmail":"{{recipientEmail}}"}

### Buyer checks participant linkage
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

### Recipient list
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/booking-participant-invitations?page=1&pageSize=20&status=PENDING
Authorization: Bearer {{recipientToken}}

### Recipient preview
GET {{baseUrl}}/booking-participant-invitations/{{invitationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{recipientToken}}

### Accept only if the declared traveller is the authenticated recipient
POST {{baseUrl}}/booking-participant-invitations/{{invitationId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{recipientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"confirmParticipantIdentity":true}

### Accepted ticket (use participantId from invitation)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/tickets/{{participantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{recipientToken}}

### Alternative to accept: decline a fresh PENDING invitation
POST {{baseUrl}}/booking-participant-invitations/{{invitationId}}/decline
Authorization: Bearer {{recipientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason":"IDENTITY_MISMATCH"}

### Alternative to accept: buyer revokes a fresh PENDING invitation
POST {{baseUrl}}/booking-participant-invitations/{{invitationId}}/revoke
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}
